-- title:
--   Square-zero universality of a generic lift over W₀[[t]]
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $W_0$ a complete discrete valuation domain which is adically complete for its maximal ideal, that ideal being generated by $q$; let $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative one-dimensional formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. its $q$-series $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ q$ (defined by iterating the law: $[0]=0$, $[n+1](X)=F_0([n](X),X)$) is a unit of $k[[X]]$ times `F₀.drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`; by the cited criterion this says $[q](X)=uX^{q^2}$ with $u$ a unit, i.e. $F_0$ has height two. Let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[[t]]$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $F_0$, and assume the genericity condition that the coefficient of $t$ in the degree-$q$ coefficient of $F_u.\mathrm{nthSeries}\ q$ is congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$. The conclusion asserts: for every commutative local artinian $W_0$-algebra $T$ with a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $T$ and which restricts along $W_0 \to T$ to $\mathrm{res}_0$, such that the square of the maximal ideal of $T$ is zero and $q = 0$ in $T$, and for every commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_T$ is $F_0$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : W_0[[t]] \to T$ such that $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ and such that there exist a formal group law $G'$ over $T$ obtained from $F_u$ by applying $\varphi$ to coefficients together with an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi : G' \to G$ (a power series with zero constant term, unit linear coefficient, compatible with the two laws) whose coefficients satisfy $\mathrm{res}_T(\mathrm{coeff}_n \psi) = \delta_{n,1}$. Uniqueness is asserted for $\varphi$ alone, not for the pair $(G', \psi)$.
--
--   This is the square-zero (first-order) case of the Lubin–Tate universality statement: the pair $(W_0[[t]], F_u)$ classifies deformations of the height-two formal group law $F_0$ over local artinian $k$-algebras with square-zero maximal ideal. It feeds [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.universal_deformation_powerSeries_of_generic_lift`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.universal_deformation_powerSeries_of_generic_lift), where the general artinian case is obtained from it.
